The crystal structure of the quintuple-layer 6512 compound consists of five consecutive NiO\(_2\) planes formed by topotactic reduction, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:tdos}(a). We label the layers as outer (\(o\))--inner (\(i\))--center (\(c\))--inner (\(i\))--outer (\(o\)), with mirror-related layers being equivalent. Density-functional calculations show that five bands predominantly derived from the Ni \(d_{x^2-y^2}\) orbitals, together with an additional La-derived band, cross the Fermi level. We therefore construct a two-dimensional five-band tight-binding (TB) model for the Ni \(d_{x^2-y^2}\) sector through Wannierization, while treating the La-derived band as a self-doping reservoir that modifies the filling of the Ni \(d_{x^2-y^2}\) bands. Details of DFT calculations are provided in Supplemental Material~\ref{appendix:dft}.

More precisely, the TB Hamiltonian $\cH_t$ is written in momentum space as
\begin{align}
    \cH_t =& \sum_{\bk,\sigma}\left[\sum_{\ell=1}^{5}\varepsilon_{\ell,\bk}c_{\bk\ell\sigma}^\dagger c_{\bk\ell\sigma}+\sum_{\langle\ell\ell^\prime\rangle} \left(\tau_{\ell\ell',\bk}c_{\bk\ell\sigma}^\dagger c_{\bk\ell'\sigma}+{\rm h.c.}\right)\right].
    \label{eq:Ht}
\end{align}
Here $c_{\bk\ell\sigma}^\dagger$ creates an electron on layer $\ell$ with momentum $\bk$ and spin $\sigma$, and $\langle\ell\ell'\rangle$ denotes the summation over adjacent layers. In the following, we also label each layer from $1$ to $5$ as indicated in Fig.~\ref{fig:tdos}(a). Consequently, the first term in Eq.~\eqref{eq:Ht} describes the intralayer dispersion, while the second describes hopping between adjacent layers, with $\tau_{oi}=\tau_{io}$ and $\tau_{ic}=\tau_{ci}$.

For each layer \(\ell\), the intralayer dispersion is written as
\begin{equation}
    \varepsilon_{\ell,\bk}
    =
    \epsilon_\ell
    +
    \sum_{m=1}^{3} t_{m\ell}\gamma_{m\bk},
\end{equation}
where \(\epsilon_\ell\) is the layer-dependent onsite energy, \(t_{m\ell}\) denotes the \(m\)-th-neighbor intralayer hopping. The corresponding lattice harmonics are $\gamma_{1\bk}=2(\cos k_x+\cos k_y)$, $\gamma_{2\bk}=4\cos k_x\cos k_y$, and $\gamma_{3\bk}=2(\cos 2k_x+\cos 2k_y)$.
Along the out-of-plane direction, we retain only hopping between adjacent NiO\(_2\) layers, parameterized as
\begin{equation}
    \tau_{\ell\ell'}(\bk)
    =
    -2t_{\perp}^{\ell\ell'}
    (\cos k_x-\cos k_y)^2,
\end{equation}
which has the same momentum dependence commonly used for multilayer cuprates \cite{Anderson1995,FengDL_PhysRevLett.86.5550}. The complete set of tight-binding parameters is listed in Table~\ref{tab:TB}.
The noninteracting band structure and Fermi surfaces are shown in Figs.~\ref{fig:tdos}(b) and \ref{fig:tdos}(c), respectively. The five Fermi-surface sheets closely resemble those of a cuprate-like tight-binding band at different hole dopings. The corresponding layer-resolved fillings are also indicated in Fig.~\ref{fig:tdos}(a), with similar doping.


