  \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{figures/fig1_beam_vs_aperture_nowin.pdf}
  \caption{Orthographic projection (top row) and aperture-plane representation (bottom row) of the beam front hemisphere at 150~MHz. Isolated (first column) and two-element (second column) models, and their complex difference (third column). White dashed circles in the aperture row indicate the dish sizes and positions. The coupling perturbation appears as a broad fringe pattern in the orthographic view but as a localized feature in the aperture view. The (Gibbs) rings in the bottom row result from Fourier transforming the finite-support orthographic projection, and do not represent real physical features.\label{fig:beam_and_aperture_coupling_comparison}}
